## WHAT THE WORK IS
**General property (binding):** *a purchase line gains ONE input member, `PurchaseLine.QuantityRule` (enum `ComponentQuantityRule { PerDevice, FixedPerGroup, Manual }`, declared in `Input/PurchaseInput.cs`, `PerDevice` first so it is `default`), trailing and optional, `[property: JsonIgnore(Condition = JsonIgnoreCondition.WhenWritingDefault)]`. The line result gains ONE member, `PurchaseLineResult.QuantityRule` (`ComponentQuantityRule?`, own `[JsonIgnore(Condition = JsonIgnoreCondition.WhenWritingNull)]`, set only when the stated rule is not `PerDevice`, last in the record). A fixed or manual line's quantity is the typed quantity, never multiplied by the fleet quantity. A per-device line is exactly X-35. A quote that states no rule, or states `PerDevice`, is byte-equal to main as a whole under all three serializers and has an equal input hash. An undefined rule value blocks the quote.* Member names are English technical; no screen word.

**The rule table (binding unless Tuesday overrides at the stamp).** Let q = the line's typed `Quantity`, N = its section's `FleetQuantity`.
| stated rule | section | counted quantity (`Quantity` on the extended line and the line result) | `QuantityPerDevice` | result `QuantityRule` |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| unset or `PerDevice` | group N | `checked(N * q)` (X-35, unchanged) | q (X-35, unchanged) | absent |
| unset or `PerDevice` | not a group | q | absent | absent |
| `FixedPerGroup` | group N (any N, also 0) | q | absent (Q-10) | `FixedPerGroup` |
| `Manual` | group N (any N, also 0) | q | absent (Q-10) | `Manual` |
| `FixedPerGroup` or `Manual` | not a group | q (figures as unset, Q-8) | absent | the stated rule |
| not a defined value | any | blocks: code `INVALID QUANTITY RULE`, target `bomLines[<n>].quantityRule`, message under Q-9; `Priced` false, `Purchase` null | | |
**Shape in code (binding):** `extended` (:171) multiplies only when `sections[l.SectionId].FleetQuantity is int n && l.QuantityRule == ComponentQuantityRule.PerDevice`; the selection at :193-195 sets `QuantityPerDevice` under the same condition; `PurchaseLineOf`'s `common` gains the carried member as `VolumeBasis` does at :572; the check goes in the `CheckPurchaseStructure` line loop beside `INVALID QUANTITY` (:365-368) with `Enum.IsDefined`, so it stops before any figure. `QuantityOf` (:51) multiplies only for a line of a group whose rule from the INPUT is `PerDevice`, written with its own expression. The `Block` local supplies the rule string; add none.
**What follows from "every later count reads the extended line" (each stated in the register and pinned, none a new site):** a fixed or manual DEVICE line counts q in the section's device quantity, the quote's device count, the tier pool (R-03) and the deal usage's pages, devices and shortfall (X-25, X-27, and with X-34 a fleet total is shared by q devices) (Q-7). A group's fee stays fee x N (X-38 reads N, not a line); a non-group section's fee counts its device quantity, so a stated rule there changes nothing. The X-39 projection reads the figures it always read.
- **Edge rows, each a test row in the NEW file, values hand-derived in a comment before the rule exists, SYNTHETIC (`SYN-*` keys, round invented values); model the fixture on `DeviceGroupTests.cs` :19-57:**
  (a) **fixed, q not 1, not N:** N 7, an option `FixedPerGroup` q 3, cost 5, percent 0.2: quantity 3 (never 21, 7 or 1), line cost 15, sell 18, `QuantityPerDevice` null, result rule `FixedPerGroup`; beside a per-device line in the same group so the section totals sum both. **(b) manual:** the same at q 5: quantity 5, never 35. **(b2) the source's own example, default rule:** a device and a reader each `PerDevice` q 1 at N 12: 12 and 12, never 144 (synthetic keys; the `E877` model name does not enter a test). **(b3) a fixed reader q 1 at N 12:** 1.
  (c) **N 1 (the shape the -255 gate found alive):** N 1 with a `FixedPerGroup` line q 2 and a `PerDevice` line q 2: both quantity 2; only the per-device line carries `QuantityPerDevice`; the carried rule tells them apart. Then N 2 with the same fixture: fixed 2, per-device 4.
  (d) **N 0 (Q-6):** per-device lines 0, fixed and manual q, section and quote totals are the fixed and manual lines' only; a stated fee on N 0 is 0 (X-38).
  (e) **Metamorphic, every figure:** at N 3, `FixedPerGroup` q 12 and `Manual` q 12 each equal `PerDevice` q 4 in every figure of the line, section and quote; JSON equal after removing exactly `quantityRule` and `quantityPerDevice` at the line and the input hash aside. Same at a book device line, so the tier pool is in the compare.
  (f) **Not a group:** each rule beside the unset twin: JSON equal after removing exactly `quantityRule` at the line; input hash differs for a stated `FixedPerGroup` and `Manual`.
  (g) **A stated `PerDevice`:** whole result raw-equal to unset and input hash equal, under InputHash's and the store's options, on a group and not.
  (h) **Flags, each with `FixedPerGroup` at N 4, q 3:** optional (`LineCost`, `LineSell` null, in no total), credit (cost and sell negative x 3), included (sell 0, cost counts x 3), sell override (override x 3), NO PRICE line (left out). One `Manual` row with credit.
  (i) **Decimals beyond cents:** a margin-on-price line (cost 10, percent 0.35 so unit sell is non-terminating), `FixedPerGroup` q 3 at N 7: line sell = the decimal product of unit sell x 3 to every digit (assert the serialised string), X-21's section total to cents from it; a `Math.Round` mutant and a mis-ordered product turn it red.
  (j) **Tier pool (R-03, money):** read `TierForPool` and the thresholds in the fixture's own terms and derive by hand: a book device `PerDevice` q 1 and a book device `FixedPerGroup` q t at N n, with n below the next tier and n + t at or above it: the higher tier's cost on BOTH lines; and N x t landing a tier further than n + t proves the row kills an "x N" mutant.
  (k) **Deal usage:** a device line `FixedPerGroup` q 2 with mono 100 per device beside a device line `PerDevice` q 1 with mono 100 at N 5, with a deal supplies model: mono pages 2 x 100 + 5 x 100 = 700, devices 7, shortfall per line x its counted quantity; the projection's monthly pages read 700. **(k2)** a `VolumeBasis.FleetTotal` line `FixedPerGroup` q 2 stating 900: pages 900 once, shared by 2 devices (X-34). State in DESIGN how the reconciler treats it (X-34's stated limit: "Not yet in the independent reconciliation"; `RecomputedUsage` :217 multiplies stated pages by `quantityOf`): name it, do not fix it.
  (l) **Fee:** a group of N 4 with a fee and a `FixedPerGroup` device line q 9: monthly fee = fee x 4, never 9, 13 or 36. A non-group section with a fee and a `Manual` device line q 3: fee x 3.
  (m) **Reconciler (the B1009-1 regression):** `QuoteReconciler.Reconcile(input, result).Agrees` true for each rule on a group and not, upfront and with a section supplies model, and with deal usage (k). **Tamper, must NOT agree (N 4, q 3, a nonzero cost, so the two counts differ):** the result calculated with the rule UNSET against the input stating `FixedPerGroup`; the same for `Manual`; the result calculated with `FixedPerGroup` against the input with the rule unset. Run on `Agrees` and on the named measure.
  (n) **Unknown refused:** `(ComponentQuantityRule)99` and `(ComponentQuantityRule)(-1)`, each on a group line, a non-group line and an optional line: `Priced` false, `Purchase` null, exactly one blocking issue with that code and target, `InputHash.Compute` does not throw on the way. A negative quantity with `FixedPerGroup` is still `INVALID QUANTITY` at `bomLines[<n>].quantity`. Under the store's options and InputHash's, the names `PerSite` and `UsageOnly` in a `PurchaseLine` JSON throw `JsonException` at deserialisation, and the integer 99 deserialises and is then refused by the engine (measure each and state it; MEASURED: 0 `Deserialize<PurchaseQuoteInput|PurchaseLine|QuoteInput>` sites in `src` and `tests`, control `Deserialize<` 19 in `src`, so no production path deserialises an engine line today).
  (o) **Byte-equal by path:** `quantityRule` absent from every line of an unset quote and a `PerDevice` quote under InputHash's and the store's options; present only at `lines[].quantityRule` on a stated line, under no section, click or usage object.
